<span class=3D"inserted-agents fr-deletable fr-tribute" id=3D"inserted-agents=
-id-3">Test Agent</span> The triage agent is misclassifying tickets that arri=
ve with a PDF attachment when the subject line is written in French. We have =
seen this happen at least four times in the last two weeks, and each time the=
 ticket ends up in the manual review queue instead of being processed automat=
ically, which defeats the whole purpose of having the agent in the first plac=
e. The customers affected were all from the Romandy region, so this looks lik=
e a language detection problem rather than a document parsing problem, but we=
 have not confirmed that yet and it would be good if someone could look at th=
e logs to understand what is actually happening before we jump to conclusions=
.<br><br>There is a second issue that may or may not be related. When the age=
nt does classify the ticket correctly and posts its private note, the note so=
metimes appears twice in the thread. It is not a duplicate in the sense of tw=
o different notes with the same content, it is literally the same note render=
ed twice, and refreshing the page makes one of them disappear. This might be =
a display problem on the Freshdesk side rather than something the agent is do=
ing wrong, but our support team has started to lose confidence in the notes b=
ecause of it, and a couple of people have told me they now double check every=
thing the agent writes, which slows them down considerably and makes the auto=
mation less useful than it should be.<br><br>Finally, and this is more of a r=
equest than a bug report, it would help a lot if the private note included a =
short line explaining why the agent reached the classification it reached. Ri=
ght now the note shows the extracted data but not the reasoning, so when the =
classification is wrong there is no way for the person reading it to understa=
nd what went wrong without going to the logs, and most of our support agents =
do not have access to the logs and would not know what to look for even if th=
ey did. A single sentence would be enough, something like which signals in th=
